---
import MissionControlSimulation from "./simulation/MissionControlSimulation.jsx";
---

<section id="interactive" class="interactive-section">
  <div class="interactive-shell container">
    <header class="interactive-header anim-reveal">
      <p class="section-kicker">Apollo 11 / Mission Control</p>
      <h1 class="section-heading">
        Mission Control:<br />Handle the 1202 Alarm
      </h1>
      <p class="interactive-briefing">
        During Apollo 11’s lunar descent, the Apollo Guidance Computer displayed 1201 and 1202 program alarms while Eagle was already approaching the Moon. The alarms did not mean the computer had completely failed. They warned that the system was overloaded and had to keep critical landing tasks alive while dropping lower-priority work.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="interactive-card card anim-reveal anim-delay-1">
      <h2>The Decision Problem</h2>
        <p>
        Mission Control had only seconds to decide whether the alarm meant
        <span class="text-purple">ABORT</span> or whether the landing could
        <span class="text-gold">CONTINUE</span>. The question was not simply
        “Is there an alarm?” The real question was: “Is the computer still
        protecting the tasks needed for guidance, navigation, and control?”
        This simulation places you inside that decision moment.
      </p>

      <p>
        The simulation begins before the decision, then guides the visitor through
        the same kind of tradeoff Mission Control had to evaluate: <span class="text-purple">whether the
        alarm was dangerous enough to stop the landing</span> or <span class="text-gold">controlled enough to
        continue</span>.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Simulation with AGC label inside the frame border -->
    <div class="terminal-frame anim-reveal anim-delay-3">
      <div class="terminal-label" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="terminal-pip"></span>
        AGC Terminal Interface Active
        <span class="terminal-pip"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="terminal-bridge">Mission briefing loaded. Continue through the console until the alarm reaches Mission Control.</p>
      <MissionControlSimulation client:load />
    </div>
    
    <div class="how-to-card anim-reveal anim-delay-2">
      <div class="how-to-title-wrap">
        <h3>Operator<br />Instructions</h3>
      </div>

      <div class="how-to-divider"></div>

      <div class="how-to-details">
        <ul>
          <li>Review the computer message, mission details, and current system status.</li>
          <li>Choose whether to abort, continue the descent, or check task priority.</li>
          <li>Prioritize the task that should receive processor attention during the overload.</li>
          <li>Monitor how each decision changes the computer load and risk level.</li>
          <li>Use the final system recommendation to decide whether to give a GO or ABORT command.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What This Shows card -->
    <article class="interactive-card card anim-reveal anim-delay-5">
      <h2><span class="text-purple">What This Shows</span></h2>
      <p>
        This simulation shows how computer architecture concepts apply in <span class="text-gold">real-time systems</span>. During an overload, the key issue is not only raw speed, but how the system prioritizes tasks, handles errors, and preserves critical operations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The activity connects the Apollo 11 1202 alarm to processor workload, task prioritization, real-time execution, and fault recovery. It shows why good architecture is <span class="text-gold">not just about performance</span>, but about keeping the right tasks running when failure pressure is high.
      </p>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const reveals = document.querySelectorAll(".anim-reveal");
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.1 }
  );
  reveals.forEach((el) => observer.observe(el));
</script>

<style>
  /* ── Section shell ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .interactive-shell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  /* ── Header ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .interactive-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .interactive-header .section-title {
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .interactive-briefing {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* ── Stacked cards ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .interactive-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .interactive-card {
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary-light) 22%, var(--border));
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.12), transparent 35%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01));
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .interactive-card h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
  }

  .interactive-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    list-style: disc;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .interactive-list li {
    padding-left: 0.25rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .interactive-card p + p {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* ── How to Play card ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .how-to-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 3fr;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary-light) 22%, var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .how-to-title-wrap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .how-to-title-wrap h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .how-to-divider {
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 60px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-primary) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .how-to-details {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .how-to-details ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: disc;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .how-to-details li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  /* ── Terminal label ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .terminal-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #7CFFB2;
    text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.35);
  }

  .terminal-pip {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #7CFFB2;
    box-shadow: 0 0 7px rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.65);
    animation: pip-blink 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes pip-blink {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
    50%       { opacity: 0.2; }
  }

  /* ── Terminal frame ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .terminal-frame {
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .terminal-frame .terminal-label {
    padding: 1rem 3rem;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  }

  .terminal-bridge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.40);
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0.35rem 1.5rem 0.45rem;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-shadow: none;
  }

  /* ── Scroll-reveal animations ────────────────────────────────── */
  .anim-reveal {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(22px);
    transition:
      opacity 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),
      transform 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .anim-reveal.is-visible {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .anim-delay-1 { transition-delay: 0.08s; }
  .anim-delay-2 { transition-delay: 0.16s; }
  .anim-delay-3 { transition-delay: 0.05s; }
  .anim-delay-4 { transition-delay: 0.1s;  }
  .anim-delay-5 { transition-delay: 0.15s; }

  /* Allow position:fixed inside terminal to reference the viewport */
  .terminal-frame.is-visible {
    transform: none;
  }

  /* ── Mobile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .how-to-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .how-to-title-wrap {
      justify-content: flex-start;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .how-to-title-wrap h3 {
      font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 5vw, 1.8rem);
    }

    .how-to-divider {
      width: 100%;
      height: 1px;
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }

  /* Simulation wrapper — no extra padding, just let the component fill */
  .interactive-card-wide {
    padding: clamp(0.5rem, 1vw, 1rem);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ── Mobile ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .interactive-card {
      padding: 1.1rem;
    }

    .interactive-card p,
    .how-to-details li {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .interactive-header .section-heading {
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 8vw, 2.2rem);
    }

    .terminal-label {
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
